refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public Io\Poll\WatcherIo\Poll\Context::add Io\Poll\Handlehandle arrayevents mixeddata&null;
Registers handle with the context, so that Io\Poll\Context::wait reports it when one of the given events occurs.
A handle can be watched only once by a context. Two StreamPollHandle objects created from the same stream count as the same handle.
The context keeps the returned Io\Poll\Watcher alive until it is removed with Io\Poll\Watcher::remove, its stream is closed, or the context is destroyed.

&reftitle.returnvalues;

 Returns the Io\Poll\Watcher that represents the
 registration.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Io\Poll\Context::add example


<?php
use Io\Poll\Context;
use Io\Poll\Event;
use Io\Poll\HandleAlreadyWatchedException;

[$reader, $writer] = stream_socket_pair(STREAM_PF_UNIX, STREAM_SOCK_STREAM, STREAM_IPPROTO_IP);

$context = new Context();
$handle = new StreamPollHandle($reader);

$watcher = $context->add($handle, [Event::Read], ['name' => 'reader']);
var_dump($watcher->isActive());
var_dump($watcher->getData());

try {
    $context->add($handle, [Event::Write]);
} catch (HandleAlreadyWatchedException $exception) {
    echo $exception->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


   &example.outputs;


bool(true)
array(1) {
  ["name"]=>
  string(6) "reader"
}
Handle already added
